{"name":"Rose Hip Tonic","hex":"#dbb9b6","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"rose","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A shrub of the genus Rosa, with red, pink, white or yellow flowers.","A flower of the rose plant."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To make rose-colored; to redden or flush.","To perfume, as with roses."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/rose"},{"term":"hip","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The outward-projecting parts of the pelvis and top of the femur and the overlying tissue.","The inclined external angle formed by the intersection of two sloping roof planes."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To use one's hips to bump into someone.","To throw (one's adversary) over one's hip (\"cross-buttock\")."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hip"},{"term":"tonic","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Pertaining to tension, especially of the muscles.","Restorative; curative; or invigorating."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A substance with medicinal properties intended to restore or invigorate.","Tonic water."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tonic"}],"entries":[{"title":"Rose hip","blocks":[{"text":"The rose hip or rosehip, also called rose haw and rose hep, is the accessory fruit of the various species of rose plant. It is typically red to orange, but ranges from dark purple to black in some species. Rose hips begin to form after pollination of flowers in spring or early summer, and ripen in late summer through autumn."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ec/Rose_hips.jpg/330px-Rose_hips.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rose_hip"},{"title":"Rose","blocks":[{"text":"A rose is either a woody perennial flowering plant of the genus Rosa, in the family Rosaceae, or the flower it bears. There are over three hundred species and tens of thousands of cultivars. The plants range in size and form, from trailing and erect shrubs to climbers up to 7 metres (23 ft) in height. Sharp prickles appear on the stems of many species. Their flowers vary in size and shape and are usually large and showy, in colours ranging from white through pinks, reds, oranges and yellows."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e6/Rosa_rubiginosa_1.jpg/330px-Rosa_rubiginosa_1.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rose"},{"title":"Hip","blocks":[{"text":"In vertebrate anatomy, the hip, or coxa in medical terminology, refers to either an anatomical region or a joint on the outer (lateral) side of the pelvis."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/9/9f/Hip.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hip"},{"title":"Rose (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Rose is the color halfway between red and magenta, whose hue corresponds to an angle of 330 degrees on the HSV/HSL color wheel."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2c/Pink-Rose-Sitia-Crete.jpg/330px-Pink-Rose-Sitia-Crete.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rose_(color)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cd/Rosa_rubiginosa_hips.jpg/330px-Rosa_rubiginosa_hips.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cd/Rosa_rubiginosa_hips.jpg/330px-Rosa_rubiginosa_hips.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Sweet-briar ssp. complete with persistent sepals at the end of the fully ripened hip, backward pointing thorns and hairs covering the pedicels and fruiting body.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARosa_rubiginosa_hips.jpg"},{"srcset":"h